    "interpretation": "The UBP Existence Unit U_e = 13824 and its cube root 24 both have rho = M(N)/N = 1/3 = 0.333333, which deviates from rho_inf = 0.196036 by 0.137297. The Existence Unit sits at the 70.4th percentile of the topological mass density \u2014 it has a higher sub-cycle density than the average integer. This is structurally meaningful: the UBP substrate (Golay code) is deliberately constructed from highly composite numbers (24 = 2^3 * 3), which have elevated phi(N)/N ratios and therefore depressed M(N)/N ratios. Wait \u2014 that's the opposite. Let me re-examine: phi(24) = 8, M(24) = 8, so M(24)/24 = 1/3 \u2248 0.333. rho_inf \u2248 0.196. So M(N)/N = 1/3 > rho_inf \u2014 the Existence Unit has HIGHER sub-cycle density than average. This is correct: highly composite numbers (small phi) have larger M(N) = floor(N/2) - phi(N)/2."
